<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ferdinand of Majorca</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1278">1278</a>–<a href="/years/1316">1316</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ferdinand of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mallorca">Majorca</a> was a prince of the Majorcan branch of the house of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a> who briefly led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catalan-company">Catalan Company</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>. He married Isabella of Sabran, heiress to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a>, and in 1315 invaded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a> to claim the principality for their son James, but was defeated and killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-manolada">Battle of Manolada</a> in 1316.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ferdinand-of-majorca.jpg" alt="Ferdinand of Majorca" width="320" height="161" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Classical Numismatic Group · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ferdinand_of_Majorca_tournois.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
